  "goodToKnow": "Der Verbrennungsmotor is the internal combustion engine; cars with one are colloquially Verbrenner. German inventors shaped it: Nikolaus Otto (four-stroke engine), Rudolf Diesel, and Carl Benz, whose 1886 Motorwagen counts as the first car. The EU's planned Verbrenner-Aus for new cars from 2035 is hotly debated in Germany. Plural: die Verbrennungsmotoren."
